CARRIED PATCH - upstream content, not ours. Provenance and why, for whoever
reads this.

Source: zephyrproject-rtos/hal_espressif PR #670, "zephyr: include GPSPI HAL
sources for ESP32 MSPI", by hitsmaxft, head a4421388, open and unmerged as of
2026-11-19. It is the companion to Zephyr PR #121107 (carried here as 0002)
and is not optional: the MSPI controller calls into the ESP-IDF SPI HAL, but
the per-SoC CMakeLists in this HAL only compiles spi_hal.c and friends when
CONFIG_ESP32_SPIM is set. An MSPI-enabled build that does not also enable the
SPI driver therefore links with undefined spi_hal_* references.

What it changes: every per-SoC CMakeLists turns
  zephyr_sources_ifdef(CONFIG_ESP32_SPIM ...)
into
  if(CONFIG_ESP32_SPIM OR CONFIG_MSPI_ESP32) zephyr_sources(...) endif()
so the HAL sources are built for either controller.

Applied to: modules/hal/espressif (this file is the whole hal_espressif patch
series; see 0003-...patch.target for the directory the applier must use).
Delete when: #670, or a merged equivalent, is in the pinned hal_espressif
revision that ships with the pinned Zephyr.
  esp-port/patches/RETIRED lists the file names that must then not come back.

Verified against: the hal_espressif revision pinned by Zephyr v4.5.0
(git apply --check clean with small line offsets, 2026-11-19).
